Expected elements: present

Presence is clean, and I checked the two items this new view could plausibly have faked. The focused control exists and is where the block says: `[data-copy].copybtn` is the identity bar's truncated hash, ring bbox x81-197 y17-45. It reflowed nothing — `Partial`'s border pixel sits at (233,20) `#ea580c` in BOTH this hydrated frame and the plain `debugger__wide__light.png`, so the upgrade is attribute-only and the P1 anti-requirement holds in pixels. No tick, no toast, no `.copied`, no failure banner, no §6.0a notice. Identity bar, `←demo` exit to the chain, `Engine loading — 18 MB` with `FETCHING` live, the `DATA` row with its `Synthetic demo data` badge and producer sentences, and all four panes are present and match the other debugger views.

Two corrections to the instrument before the finding, because the block oversells its own defect. (1) The ring is **not** a UA default. It samples `#3b82f6` in light and `#60a5fa` in dark — `--bt-focus-ring`, applied by `styles.nim:114`'s `:where(...,[tabindex]):focus-visible`, declared in `web.tokens.json:152` as "One focus treatment for BOTH registers", with the dark rung documented at `DESIGN-DIVERGENCES-WEB.md:134`. So "a UA focus ring and nothing else" is false, and the watch-for "does it survive the dark register at all" is answered in the token file before any image is taken. (2) The MUST-SHOW asserts `.dbgid`/`.mdhash` render `0x0858d644…22e67fb2`. That is `debugger--testnet`'s aztec-testnet hash (`hydration-divergence.json:171`); this route is `/demo/tx/0xb636167a…d46359/debug` and renders `0xb63616…6359`. Applied literally that MUST-SHOW manufactures a false P1 REPLACED. Both belong in the block, not in the ledger — the defect is real, it is just smaller than advertised, which is why my finding is P2 and not P1.

Weakest element: the focused control itself. It is the only thing in a 62px bar of rounded controls that is a square-cornered rectangle, and the one thing the page calls a button while specifying nothing about it.

